# The ledger of `diff`: what Python's `difflib` (3.15), Go's `internal/diff`
# (1.27) and go-diff (github.com/sergi/go-diff v1.4.5, `diffmatchpatch`), and
# Rust's `similar` (2.x) let a program do with the differences of two lists
# or texts, one block per capability, and what Rebel answers. Go's own
# standard library offers no difference beyond `internal/diff`, which a
# program outside Go cannot import; go-diff stands for Go's side.
#
# The lists are this machine's, 2026-11-17: `dir(difflib)` and of its
# classes; `go doc -all internal/diff` and `go doc -all` of `diffmatchpatch`
# fetched into the scratch folder; the items of `cargo doc -p similar` (its
# functions, structs, enums and their methods), fetched the same way.
#
# The differential, 2026-11-17, a program printing Rebel's answers beside
# Python run on generated texts: 3,120 pairs of texts by characters (alphabets
# of 2 to 10 letters, letters of two and three bytes among them, 120 pairs of
# 190 to 420 characters past the junk heuristic), each Myers script checked
# shortest against a longest common subsequence and checked to turn one text
# into the other, each Ratcliff script equal to `get_opcodes`, each patience
# script checked to turn one into the other, `ratio`, `quick_ratio`,
# `real_quick_ratio` and `get_matching_blocks` equal to Python's; 400 calls of
# `get_close_matches` equal; 300 pairs of files at contexts 0 to 5 written
# byte for byte as Python's `unified_diff` and `context_diff` write them from
# the Ratcliff script, and, from Myers's, the same number of changed lines as
# the system's `diff -u` (Apple's, after FreeBSD) in every pair and the same
# bytes in 243 of 300, where the two shortest scripts differ only in which of
# two equal lines they keep. 50,000 lines with 300 changes take 0.09 s and 21
# MB by Myers.

capability edits/lines  the edit script of two lists of lines
  heroes  diff.edits, diff.lines_of, diff.Op, diff.Tag
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffLinesToChars, DiffMatchPatch.DiffLinesToRunes, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCharsToLines, Diff, Operation, DiffDelete, DiffInsert, DiffEqual, Operation.String
  rust    TextDiff::from_lines, TextDiffConfig::diff_lines, utils::diff_lines, DiffOp, DiffTag, DiffOp::tag, DiffOp::old_range, DiffOp::new_range, DiffOp::as_tag_tuple, TextDiff::ops
  python  SequenceMatcher.get_opcodes
  note    the script is Myers's shortest, as GNU diff, go-diff and `similar` find it, where Python's is Ratcliff and Obershelp's (edits/algorithm). Its runs are Python's opcodes, ranges into both lists with the tags equal, delete, insert and replace; go-diff holds the text of each run instead, and a program reads the text from the ranges. A line keeps its line feed, as `similar`'s lines do

capability edits/words  the edit script of two texts by words
  heroes  diff.words_of, diff.edits
  go      -
  rust    TextDiff::from_words, TextDiff::from_unicode_words, TextDiffConfig::diff_words, TextDiffConfig::diff_unicode_words, utils::diff_words, utils::diff_unicode_words
  python  -
  note    a word and each run of white space between words are elements, as `similar`'s `from_words` cuts; Unicode's word boundaries (`from_unicode_words`) are `unicode/segment`'s, and its words go to `edits` the same way

capability edits/characters  the edit script of two texts by characters
  heroes  diff.edits
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffMain, DiffMatchPatch.DiffMainRunes
  rust    TextDiff::from_chars, TextDiffConfig::diff_chars, utils::diff_chars
  python  SequenceMatcher.get_opcodes
  note    `edits(old: a.chars(), new: b.chars())`; grapheme clusters (`similar`'s `from_graphemes`) are `unicode/segment`'s, given the same way

capability edits/bytes  the edit script of two lists of bytes
  heroes  diff.edits_of_bytes
  go      -
  rust    TextDiff::from_slices, TextDiffConfig::diff_slices, utils::diff_slices
  python  diff_bytes
  note    -

capability edits/any  the edit script of two lists of any values
  heroes  diff.edits_by
  go      -
  rust    capture_diff_slices, capture_diff, algorithms::diff, algorithms::diff_slices, algorithms::Capture, algorithms::DiffHook, algorithms::NoFinishHook, algorithms::Replace, algorithms::Compact, algorithms::IdentifyDistinct
  python  SequenceMatcher, SequenceMatcher.set_seqs, SequenceMatcher.set_seq1, SequenceMatcher.set_seq2
  note    equality is a function the program passes, since a value of a type parameter has no `==`; `similar`'s hooks, which a trait's methods receive one edit at a time, are the script walked as a list

capability edits/algorithm  the algorithm that finds the script: Myers's, patience, or Python's
  heroes  diff.edits_with, diff.Algorithm, diff.Options.algorithm
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffBisect, DiffMatchPatch.DiffHalfMatch, Diff
  rust    Algorithm, Algorithm::Myers, Algorithm::Patience, Algorithm::Lcs, TextDiff::algorithm, TextDiffConfig::algorithm, algorithms::myers, algorithms::patience, algorithms::lcs
  python  SequenceMatcher.get_opcodes
  note    Myers's in linear space by default, the shortest script; patience as `similar`'s, unique lines matched first in their longest common order, Myers's between them; Ratcliff and Obershelp's, the same script as Python's `get_opcodes` in every one of 3,120 pairs. Go's `internal/diff` writes an anchored diff, which is patience. `similar`'s `Lcs` is a third way to a script of the same length as Myers's, not offered; go-diff's half-match speed-up is not taken

capability edits/deadline  a time after which a comparison stops and answers a script that is not the shortest
  heroes  pending
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffTimeout
  rust    TextDiffConfig::deadline, TextDiffConfig::timeout, capture_diff_deadline, capture_diff_slices_deadline, algorithms::diff_deadline, algorithms::diff_slices_deadline, TextDiff::iter_inline_changes_deadline
  python  -
  note    Myers's cost is O((N+M)D), so two long texts with nothing in common take time in the product of their lengths; a bound on D, as GNU diff's heuristics bound it, is the way, not done in this round

capability edits/distance  how many elements a script changes
  heroes  diff.distance
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffLevenshtein
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    a replace counts its longer side, as go-diff counts; from Myers's script of characters it is the Levenshtein distance

capability edits/sides  the old and the new text read back from a script
  heroes  refused: a run holds ranges into the two lists, which the program has; `old.slice(from: op.old_from, to: op.old_to)` is either side of a run
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffText1, DiffMatchPatch.DiffText2, DiffMatchPatch.DiffXIndex
  rust    TextDiff::old_slices, TextDiff::new_slices, DiffOp::iter_slices, utils::TextDiffRemapper
  python  restore
  note    go-diff's `DiffXIndex` maps a place in the old text to the new: the runs' ranges answer it

capability edits/changes  the script walked element by element, each with its old and new index
  heroes  diff.edits
  go      -
  rust    TextDiff::iter_changes, TextDiff::iter_all_changes, DiffOp::iter_changes, Change, Change::tag, Change::old_index, Change::new_index, Change::value, Change::missing_newline, ChangeTag
  python  -
  note    a run's ranges give each element and its index; `missing_newline` is a last line without its line feed, which `lines_of` keeps visible

capability edits/inline  the words or characters that changed inside changed lines
  heroes  pending
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupSemantic, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupSemanticLossless
  rust    TextDiff::iter_inline_changes, InlineChange, InlineChange::values, InlineChange::iter_strings_lossy, InlineChange::tag
  python  Differ, Differ.compare, ndiff
  note    a second difference by words inside each replaced pair of lines, and Python's `?` guide lines; not done in this round

capability edits/cleanup  a script made easier to read by moving and merging its edits
  heroes  pending
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupSemantic, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupSemanticLossless, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupEfficiency, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCleanupMerge, DiffMatchPatch.DiffEditCost, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCommonOverlap
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    go-diff's heuristics for character differences shown to people; a script with ranges is already merged (no two equal runs touch, a delete and an insert side by side are one replace)

capability edits/common  the length of the common beginning and end of two texts
  heroes  refused: `strings` and `lists` answer the common beginning (`lists.has_prefix` by length), and `edits` matches both ends first itself
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffCommonPrefix, DiffMatchPatch.DiffCommonSuffix
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    -

capability edits/hunks  a script cut into hunks with lines of context
  heroes  diff.hunks
  go      -
  rust    TextDiff::grouped_ops, group_diff_ops, udiff::UnifiedDiff::iter_hunks, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk::ops, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk::iter_changes
  python  SequenceMatcher.get_grouped_opcodes
  note    as Python cuts them: a run of more than twice the context ends a hunk, and the first and last equal runs are cut to the context

capability output/unified  two lists of lines written in the unified format
  heroes  diff.format_unified, diff.Options, diff.default_options
  go      internal/diff.Diff
  rust    TextDiff::unified_diff, udiff::unified_diff, udiff::UnifiedDiff, udiff::UnifiedDiff::context_radius, udiff::UnifiedDiff::header, udiff::UnifiedDiff::missing_newline_hint, udiff::UnifiedDiff::from_text_diff, udiff::UnifiedDiff::to_writer, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk::header, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk::to_writer, udiff::UnifiedDiffHunk::missing_newline_hint, udiff::UnifiedHunkHeader
  python  unified_diff
  note    the headers and ranges exact: byte for byte as Python's `unified_diff` writes from the same script in 300 of 300 pairs, and as the system's `diff -u` writes wherever the two shortest scripts agree, `\ No newline at end of file` included, which Python leaves out. Python's `lineterm` is the line feed alone; its colour (`color=`, `get_theme`, `can_colorize`) is `term`'s

capability output/context  two lists of lines written in the context format
  heroes  diff.format_context
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  context_diff
  note    as Python's `context_diff` and `diff -c` write it, the side of a hunk with no change writing its range alone

capability output/html  a difference written as an HTML table or with HTML marks
  heroes  refused: the edit script and `html.escape` make any page a program means; one table layout fixed here would be one more template to keep
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffPrettyHtml
  rust    -
  python  HtmlDiff, HtmlDiff.make_file, HtmlDiff.make_table
  note    -

capability output/terminal  a difference written with terminal colours
  heroes  refused: colours are `term`'s; the script and `term`'s styles write it
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffPrettyText
  rust    -
  python  can_colorize, get_theme
  note    -

capability output/delta  a script written in go-diff's compact delta and read back
  heroes  refused: one library's own encoding, which no other reads; a unified difference is the exchange format
  go      DiffMatchPatch.DiffToDelta, DiffMatchPatch.DiffFromDelta
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    -

