capability similarity/ratio  how alike two lists are, as Python measures it
  heroes  diff.ratio
  go      -
  rust    TextDiff::ratio, get_diff_ratio
  python  SequenceMatcher.ratio
  note    Ratcliff and Obershelp's matching, another algorithm than the script's, with Python's automatic junk (an element in more than one in a hundred places of a second list of 200 or more starts no match); equal to Python's in every one of 3,120 pairs. `similar`'s `ratio` was not asked

capability similarity/bounds  quick upper bounds of the ratio
  heroes  diff.quick_ratio, diff.real_quick_ratio
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  SequenceMatcher.quick_ratio, SequenceMatcher.real_quick_ratio
  note    -

capability similarity/blocks  the runs two lists share, and the longest of them
  heroes  diff.matching_blocks, diff.longest_match, diff.Block
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  SequenceMatcher.get_matching_blocks, SequenceMatcher.find_longest_match, Match
  note    the last block is Python's `(len(a), len(b), 0)`

capability similarity/junk  elements a program marks as junk, which start no match
  heroes  pending
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  SequenceMatcher(isjunk=), SequenceMatcher(autojunk=), IS_LINE_JUNK, IS_CHARACTER_JUNK
  note    the automatic heuristic is always on, as Python's default; a junk function given by the program and the switch are not done in this round

capability similarity/close  the texts of a list most like a word
  heroes  diff.close_matches
  go      -
  rust    get_close_matches, text::get_close_matches
  python  get_close_matches
  note    Python's answers in 400 of 400 calls: ratio by characters, best first, ties by the later text

dropped
  python  GenericAlias: a typing name `difflib` imports, not its own
  go      DiffMatchPatch, New: the settings a method reads; here each setting is a parameter or a field of `Options`
  go      FOUR_BYTE_BITS, ONE_BYTE_BITS, THREE_BYTE_BITS, TWO_BYTE_BITS, UNICODE_INVALID_RANGE_START, UNICODE_INVALID_RANGE_END, UNICODE_INVALID_RANGE_DELTA, UNICODE_RANGE_MAX: constants of go-diff's own encoding of lines as runes
  rust    TextDiff::configure, TextDiffConfig::default, TextDiff::newline_terminated, TextDiffConfig::newline_terminated, TextDiff::from: builders of the configuration; `lines_of` keeps the line feed of every line
  rust    Change::value_ref, Change::value_mut, Change::to_string_lossy, Change::as_str, DiffOp::apply_to_hook, algorithms::Capture::into_ops, algorithms::Capture::into_grouped_ops, algorithms::Compact::into_inner, the DiffableStr and DiffableStrRef traits, and the traits every type derives: borrowing and conversions a value here does not need
